Drydock is an independent, from-scratch implementation of a Docker container
auto-updater. Its design is informed by the behaviour and documentation of
Watchtower (https://github.com/containrrr/watchtower), Copyright The
Watchtower Authors, which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

No Watchtower source code is included in this repository.

Watchtower itself is no longer maintained (archived December 2025); Drydock was
written to carry the idea forward with health-gated updates, automatic
rollback, persistent history, per-container schedules, and a modern API.
